{"name":"Chenin","hex":"#dec371","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Chenin blanc","blocks":[{"text":"Chenin blanc is a white wine grape variety from the Loire Valley of France. Its high acidity means it can be used to make varieties from sparkling wines to well-balanced dessert wines, although it can produce very bland, neutral wines if the vine's natural vigor is not controlled. Outside the Loire, it is found in most of the New World wine regions; it is the most widely planted variety in South Africa, where it was historically also known as Steen. The grape may have been one of the first to be grown in South Africa by Jan van Riebeeck in 1655, or it may have come to that country with Huguenots fleeing France after the revocation of the Edict of Nantes in 1685. Chenin blanc was often misidentified in Australia, as well, so tracing its early history in the country is not easy. It may have been introduced in James Busby's collection of 1832, but C. Waterhouse was growing Steen at Highercombe in Houghton, South Australia, by 1862."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Rochecorbon_-_Vignoble_-_02.jpg/330px-Rochecorbon_-_Vignoble_-_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chenin_blanc","wikidata":"Q1070101"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Rabelais_by_dore.jpg/500px-Rabelais_by_dore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Rabelais_by_dore.jpg/500px-Rabelais_by_dore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The works of French writer François Rabelais indicate that Chenin blanc was a major grape in the Loire Valley by the 16th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARabelais_by_dore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg/500px-Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg/1280px-Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg/500px-Sauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chenin blanc grapes, like these Sauvignon blanc grapes pictured, are highly sensitive to developing noble rot, which produces a unique style of wine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASauternes_noble_rot_grapes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Grape_gathering.jpg/500px-Grape_gathering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Grape_gathering.jpg/1280px-Grape_gathering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Grape_gathering.jpg/500px-Grape_gathering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Producers often harvest Chenin blanc by hand in a succession of pickings known as \"tries\". The grapes may be harvested as whole clusters or individual berries.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrape_gathering.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0d/Vouvray_Sparkling_Chenin_blanc_wine.JPG/330px-Vouvray_Sparkling_Chenin_blanc_wine.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0d/Vouvray_Sparkling_Chenin_blanc_wine.JPG/330px-Vouvray_Sparkling_Chenin_blanc_wine.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chenin blanc can be made in a variety of styles, such as this sparkling wine from Vouvray.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVouvray_Sparkling_Chenin_blanc_wine.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg/500px-Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg/1280px-Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg/500px-Stellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"South African Chenin blancs tend to emphasize more tropical fruit flavors than their Loire counterparts.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStellenbosch_Chenin_blanc.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Washington_Chenin.jpg/500px-Washington_Chenin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Washington_Chenin.jpg/1280px-Washington_Chenin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Washington_Chenin.jpg/500px-Washington_Chenin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Chenin blanc from Washington","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWashington_Chenin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Two_Chenin_Blanc_wines_in_glass.jpg/500px-Two_Chenin_Blanc_wines_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Two_Chenin_Blanc_wines_in_glass.jpg/1280px-Two_C